-- lib/meaning.cub — meaning computed from the record (docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub, §§2–4),
-- at the level of characters, with nothing added. The record is every text the source holds (each
-- module as the file it is) and every turn said since. An occurrence is an event of the record; the
-- only identification is equality of characters. The present context is the turn; a past occurrence is
-- selected exactly when its context is identified with the present one, and the most context identified
-- is the longest end of the turn the record holds (context resolves by shrinking the fiber, never by
-- weighting). The meaning is the family of what followed the selected occurrences, each to the end of
-- its line, equal continuations being one: where they all agree the meaning is determinate and is
-- printed once; where they part, the family is printed as it is, every branch.
-- Memory is local (memory-is-local): no process holds the whole record. It is read one text at a time,
-- each held as its bytes, and the search runs over the bytes in compiled code (#jit). The longest end of
-- the turn a text holds is the longest prefix of the reversed turn the reversed text holds, which the
-- Knuth–Morris–Pratt automaton of the reversed turn finds in one pass: Θ(ℓ + m) for a text of ℓ bytes and
-- a turn of m, so a query is Θ(n + T·m) over the n bytes of the T texts, holding one text at a time. The
-- end considered is the turn's last 1024 bytes.
-- Used by `hyperactive chat` (lib/chat.cub) and by the server's /chat and /api/meaning, which hold it in
-- their running process.
